<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE LAUNCHER ICON'S GROUND, as a RAMP rather than a flat fill.

  `ic_launcher.xml` used to say the background was "a flat colour rather than
  a bitmap: one hex to change, and nothing to re-render at five densities when
  the brand moves". That argument was about a BITMAP, and it still holds —
  this is a vector shape, so there is nothing to re-render and still one place
  to change.

  It is a ramp because the supplied artwork is: a rounded square running from
  a deep teal at the top-left to a near-black teal at the bottom-right. A flat
  fill of the lighter end is a different logo.

  `startColor` is `@color/ic_launcher_background`, so the hex still lives in
  `colors.xml` beside the window colour it has to stay in the same family as —
  and `splashAndIntro.test.ts` can still read it there.

  Angle 315: Android measures anticlockwise from "left to right", so 315 runs
  top-left to bottom-right. 45 would run the artwork backwards.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" android:shape="rectangle">
    <gradient
        android:type="linear"
        android:angle="315"
        android:startColor="@color/ic_launcher_background"
        android:endColor="#062E33" />
</shape>
